+---
+title: 'Application-form stepper (F1) + field diet (F4) + upload copy (F5)'
+type: 'feature'
+created: '2026-08-01'
+status: 'in-review'
+baseline_commit: 'd85a0ed1aebcb582bd43ac0f7c71fc0646ea1ebb'
+review_loop_iteration: 0
+context: []
+---
+
+<frozen-after-approval reason="human-owned intent — do not modify unless human renegotiates">
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** The public `/apply/:code` form renders ~36 controls on one long page (80% mobile) and abandons at ~89%: daunt at first render plus an unguided document wall. Spec of record: `_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/problem-solving-application-form-completion-2026-07-31.md` (F1/F4/F5 rows, Wave 1 build pack).
+
+**Approach:** Progressive-enhancement stepper over the existing 8 SSR sections (named sticky progress, per-step validation gating, single POST, no-JS fallback stays the long form), plus field diet (drop the optional non-scoring `listing_source` select; collapse the optional address cluster into `<details>`) and camera-roll-friendly per-slot upload helper copy.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- `data-section-id` values + section DOM order unchanged (funnel keys off them); `apply_analytics.js` and `form.js` untouched.
+- Single POST at the end; submit/consent/honeypot/timing machinery untouched.
+- No-JS fallback: SSR renders all 8 sections visible and submittable as today.
+- Scoring inputs untouched — no removing/renaming/re-requiring any field in `ai_client.gleam`'s payload (address cluster + `eircode` stay, only visually collapsed).
+- `view_prep_block()` and its `F3-SEAM` comment byte-untouched (follow-up C seam).
+- Applicant-facing strings live in `server/src/copy.gleam`; brand voice (calm, specific; never "Error/Failed/Retry").
+- `listing_source` stays accepted server-side: DB column, `is_valid_listing_source`, `error_summary` label, and `work_income.listing_source_options` const + parity test remain (cached pages may still post it).
+
+**Ask First:**
+- Reintroducing `listing_source` post-submit (confirmation widget + endpoint) — deferred follow-up, not this PR.
+- Any change to the prep block copy or the one-visit line.
+
+**Never:**
+- Per-section persistence, localStorage drafts, magic continue links (follow-up C's job).
+- Dropping the `listing_source` column or rejecting the field server-side.
+- A JS-generated "review summary" of entered values (rejected: PII-echo + scope; Back navigation covers review).
+- Merging the PR.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Advance | Step's visible required filled, Continue | Next section shown, others `hidden`; progress "Step N of 8 — Name"; `rt:form-step-changed` `{step_index, section_id, total}`; focus legend, scroll to top of section | N/A |
+| Gating | Visible required empty, Continue | Stay; `.has-error` + short brand-voice message in the field's `.field-error`; focus first invalid | Clears on input/next pass |
+| Radio group | Required, none checked | Blocks; valid when any visible member checked | Same inline pattern |
+| Conditional hidden | Required control inside `hidden` conditional (guarantor off, pet details…) | Skipped by gating (visibility walk mirrors apply_analytics) | N/A |
+| Dynamic required | `employment_status=employed` (employer fields gain `required`) | Empty visible employer field blocks | Existing toggle supplies `required` |
+| Error re-render | `data-apply-page="form-errors"` | Stepper starts at first `.has-error` section; error-summary anchor clicks switch step + focus target; banner keeps initial focus | Falls back to step 1 |
+| No JS | Script absent/blocked | All 8 sections visible; one POST submits; server validation authoritative | Existing path |
+| Files across steps | Files chosen, then Back/Continue | Inputs keep `FileList`; preflight/submit unchanged | Server caps authoritative |
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
+
+## Code Map
+
+- `server/priv/static/form_stepper.js` — NEW stepper module (CommonJS-testable internals like apply_analytics.js).
+- `server/priv/static/apply_analytics.js` / `form.js` — gating rules to mirror; coexistence. DO NOT EDIT.
+- `server/priv/static/form.css` — stepper chrome, `.optional-cluster`, `.form-section[hidden]` guard, `scroll-margin-top`.
+- `server/src/application/form_view.gleam` + `form_pages.gleam` — add `/static/form_stepper.js` defer script after form.js (pristine + error pages).
+- `server/src/application/form_sections/work_income.gleam` — remove `listing_source` select render; keep + re-comment the const.
+- `server/src/application/form_sections/situation.gleam` — `<details class="optional-cluster">` around the 4 address fields (open when any prefilled).
+- `server/src/application/form_sections/documents.gleam` + `server/src/copy.gleam` — F5 per-slot helpers (proof-of-income + co-applicant slots gain helpers; ref slots extended).
+- `server/src/ai/ai_client.gleam` — reference only: payload surface to keep diff-empty.
+- `scripts/js-tests/form_stepper.test.js` — NEW node tests (`make test-js` globs `*.test.js`).
+- `server/test/application/form_view_test.gleam` — SSR pins.
+
+## Tasks & Acceptance
+
+**Execution:**
+- [x] `server/priv/static/form_stepper.js` — create: init on `data-apply-page` `form`|`form-errors`; sections from `[data-section-id]`; sticky progress (aria-live text + aria-hidden segments, names from `legend.section-title`); per-section nav (Back steps 2–8, Continue 1–7, `type="button"`); Continue gates on visible-required-filled (radio any-checked, checkbox checked, file `files.length`, else trimmed non-empty; skip hidden/disabled); step change → event + legend focus (`tabindex=-1`) + scrollIntoView; form-errors → start at first-error section, route summary anchors through step switch; rewrite review hint to Back-based copy; no-op cleanly when markers absent.
+- [x] `server/priv/static/form.css` — sticky `.stepper-progress` (mobile-tuned), segments, `.stepper-nav` rows (44px targets), `.form-section[hidden]{display:none}`, `.optional-cluster` styles.
+- [x] `server/src/application/form_view.gleam` + `form_pages.gleam` — script tags.
+- [x] `server/src/application/form_sections/work_income.gleam` — drop the select.
+- [x] `server/src/application/form_sections/situation.gleam` — details-collapse the address cluster.
+- [x] `server/src/copy.gleam` + `form_sections/documents.gleam` — F5 strings wired into every slot.
+- [x] `scripts/js-tests/form_stepper.test.js` — unit-test every I/O-matrix row + no-op guards + event payload.
+- [x] `server/test/application/form_view_test.gleam` — pin: 8 sections visible (no `hidden` on fieldsets), ids in order, details closed pristine/open prefilled, `listing_source` absent, F5 helpers present, script tag present, prep block + F3-SEAM substring intact.
+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given JS on, when Continue passes gating, then the next section shows, progress reads "Step N of 8 — <Name>", and `rt:form-step-changed` fires with the new `section_id`.
+- Given a visible required field empty, when Continue is clicked, then navigation blocks with an inline brand-voice message and focus on the first invalid field.
+- Given JS disabled, when the page loads, then all 8 sections render visible and one POST submits the form (existing integration path green).
+- Given an error re-render, when the page loads, then the stepper starts at the first error's section and summary links switch steps + focus the field.
+- Given the stepper active, then `application_form_section_entered/completed/abandoned` still fire with unchanged `section_id`s (observer sees only shown sections).
+- Given F4, then `listing_source` is absent from the pristine HTML while the handler still accepts it (parity test green), and the collapsed address cluster still submits.
+- Given the branch diff, then `server/src/ai/` is unchanged (scoring-input proof in PR).
+
+## Design Notes
+
+- Gating duplicates ~30 lines of apply_analytics' visibility rules with a keep-in-sync comment — plain static JS has no cross-file imports, and apply_analytics.js must stay untouched.
+- `listing_source` dropped (not post-submit): spec grants either; a confirmation widget needs a new public mutation endpoint + application-identity token — large surface for a "small" fold-in. Ops digest degrades to `(unknown)` on new rows; PostHog referrers still show channel. Open follow-up.
+- `rt:form-step-changed` is the documented seam for follow-up C's save-on-section-change.
+- Stepper runs on the error page because anchor links into `hidden` sections are dead ends otherwise; it never steals the banner's first focus.
+
+## Verification
+
+**Commands:**
+- `make format && make test && make build` — all green (test-js runs the new node tests).
+- `make test-db-up && make test-integration` — green (submit path unchanged).
+- `git diff origin/develop -- server/src/ai/` — empty (scoring-input proof).
+- `grep -c 'listing_source' <(curl -s localhost:4000/apply/<code>)` on `make dev` — 0.
+
+**Manual checks (if no CLI):**
+- `make dev` + browser (mobile ~390px + desktop): fill → gate blocks empty required → Back preserves values/files → consent → submit → confirmation; bfcache restore keeps stepper consistent; sticky progress visible on mobile scroll.
